<urn:usf:contract:delivery-environment:1> <urn:usf:predicate:objective> "Give the environment ladder semantic meaning, pin every verdict to the environment that produced it, and add the nine delivery obligations the existing sixty-seven do not express, so that a product's route to production is derivable rather than narrated." <urn:usf:graph:delivery-environment> .
<urn:usf:contract:delivery-environment:1> <urn:usf:predicate:objectiveEvidence> "The seven environments existed as bare type assertions with no posture, ordering or evidence requirements, and their applicability records carried only \"required\" or \"reserved\". Nothing prevented a development verdict from answering a production question because nothing said the rungs differed." <urn:usf:graph:delivery-environment> .
<urn:usf:contract:delivery-environment:1> <urn:usf:predicate:constructionRouteConstraint> "Local, hermetic and deterministic. This contract declares vocabulary and invariants only: it contacts no provider, reads no credential, provisions no resource and names no vendor." <urn:usf:graph:delivery-environment> .
