<urn:usf:contract:delivery-environment:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "This contract selects no vendor, provisions nothing and deploys nothing. It makes the difference between rungs checkable; instantiating any environment is separate work with separate evidence." <urn:usf:graph:delivery-environment> .
<urn:usf:contract:delivery-environment:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "Sixty-seven delivery contracts already existed. Nine were added because reconciliation found nothing covering static asset serving, edge execution, public ingress, response-header policy, CDN cache policy, health and readiness, deployment, rollback or release provenance. The other three candidates were dropped as duplicates." <urn:usf:graph:delivery-environment> .
<urn:usf:contract:delivery-environment:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "Giving the rungs meaning does not create a promotion platform. A gate is a predicate over evidence, evaluated where the evidence already lives." <urn:usf:graph:delivery-environment> .
